$\begin{align}
\dfrac{a^{7}}{a^6}&=\dfrac{\overbrace{\cancel a\cdot \cancel a\cdot \cancel a\cdot \cancel a\cdot \cancel a\cdot \cancel a\cdot a}^\text{7 times}}{\underbrace{\cancel a\cdot \cancel a\cdot \cancel a\cdot \cancel a\cdot \cancel a\cdot \cancel a}_\text{6 times}}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{a}_\text{1 time}
\\\\
\end{align}$

When powers have the same base $\dfrac{x^m}{x^n}=x^{m-n}$. 

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{a^{7}}{a^6}&=a^{7-6}
\\\\
&=a^1
\end{align}$
